{
  "title": "79: al-Naazea'at النازعات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالنّٰزِعٰتِ غَرْقًا ۙ‏(1)\n\nBy the (angels) who tear out (the souls of the wicked) with violence; \nوَّالنّٰشِطٰتِ نَشْطًا ۙ‏(2)\n\nBy those who gently draw out (the souls of the blessed); \nوَّالسّٰبِحٰتِ سَبْحًا ۙ‏(3)\n\nAnd by those who glide along (on errands of mercy), \nفَالسّٰبِقٰتِ سَبْقًا ۙ‏(4)\n\nThen press forward as in a race, \nفَالْمُدَبِّرٰتِ اَمْرًا‌ ۘ‏(5)\n\nThen arrange to do (the Commands of their Lord), \nيَوْمَ تَرْجُفُ الرَّاجِفَةُ ۙ‏(6)\n\nOne Day everything that can be in commotion will be in violent commotion, \nتَتْبَعُهَا الرَّادِفَةُ ؕ‏(7)\n\nFollowed by oft-repeated (commotions): \nقُلُوْبٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ وَّاجِفَةٌ ۙ‏(8)\n\nHearts that Day will be in agitation; \nاَبْصَارُهَا خَاشِعَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(9)\n\nCast down will be (their owners') eyes. \nيَقُوْلُوْنَ ءَاِنَّا لَمَرْدُوْدُوْنَ فِى الْحَافِرَةِ ؕ‏(10)\n\nThey say (now): “What! shall we indeed be returned to (our) former state? \nءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا نَّخِرَةً ؕ‏(11)\n\n“What! - when we shall have become rotten bones?” \nقَالُوْا تِلْكَ اِذًا كَرَّةٌ خَاسِرَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(12)\n\nThey say: “It would, in that case, be a return with loss!” \nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ ۙ‏(13)\n\nBut verily, it will be but a single (Compelling) Cry, \nفَاِذَا هُمْ بِالسَّاهِرَةِ ؕ‏(14)\n\nWhen, behold, they will be in the (full) awakening (to Judgment). \nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ مُوْسٰى‌ۘ‏(15)\n\nHas the story of Moses reached thee? \nاِذْ نَادٰٮهُ رَبُّهٗ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى‌ۚ‏(16)\n\nBehold, thy Lord did call to him in the sacred valley of Tuwa:- \nاِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى ۖ‏(17)\n\n“Go thou to Pharaoh for he has indeed transgressed all bounds: \nفَقُلْ هَلْ لَّكَ اِلٰٓى اَنْ تَزَكّٰى ۙ‏(18)\n\n“And say to him, 'Wouldst thou that thou shouldst be purified (from sin)? \nوَاَهْدِيَكَ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ فَتَخْشٰى‌ۚ‏(19)\n\n“'And that I guide thee to thy Lord, so thou shouldst fear Him?'“ \nفَاَرٰٮهُ الْاٰيَةَ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(20)\n\nThen did (Moses) show him the Great Sign. \nفَكَذَّبَ وَعَصٰى ۖ‏(21)\n\nBut (Pharaoh) rejected it and disobeyed (guidance); \nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ يَسْعٰىۖ‏(22)\n\nFurther, he turned his back, striving hard (against Allah). \nفَحَشَرَ فَنَادٰىۖ‏(23)\n\nThen he collected (his men) and made a proclamation, \nفَقَالَ اَنَا رَبُّكُمُ الْاَعْلٰى ۖ‏(24)\n\nSaying, “I am your Lord, Most High”. \nفَاَخَذَهُ اللّٰهُ نَڪَالَ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَالْاُوْلٰى ؕ‏(25)\n\nBut Allah did punish him, (and made an) example of him, - in the Hereafter, as in this life. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِّمَنْ يَّخْشٰىؕ‏(26)\n\nVerily in this is an instructive warning for whosoever feareth (Allah). \nءَاَنْتُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمِ السَّمَآءُ‌ ؕ بَنٰٮهَا‏(27)\n\nWhat! Are ye the more difficult to create or the heaven (above)? (Allah) hath constructed it: \nرَفَعَ سَمْكَهَا فَسَوَّٮهَا ۙ‏(28)\n\nOn high hath He raised its canopy, and He hath given it order and perfection. \nوَ اَغْطَشَ لَيْلَهَا وَاَخْرَجَ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(29)\n\nIts night doth He endow with darkness, and its splendour doth He bring out (with light). \nوَالْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ دَحٰٮهَا ؕ‏(30)\n\nAnd the earth, moreover, hath He extended (to a wide expanse); \nاَخْرَجَ مِنْهَا مَآءَهَا وَمَرْعٰٮهَا‏(31)\n\nHe draweth out therefrom its moisture and its pasture; \nوَالْجِبَالَ اَرْسٰٮهَا ۙ‏(32)\n\nAnd the mountains hath He firmly fixed;- \nمَتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِاَنْعَامِكُمْؕ‏(33)\n\nFor use and convenience to you and your cattle. \nفَاِذَا جَآءَتِ الطَّآمَّةُ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(34)\n\nTherefore, when there comes the great, overwhelming (Event), \nيَوْمَ يَتَذَكَّرُ الْاِنْسَانُ مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(35)\n\nThe Day when man shall remember (all) that he strove for, \nوَبُرِّزَتِ الْجَحِيْمُ لِمَنْ يَّرٰى‏(36)\n\nAnd Hell-Fire shall be placed in full view for (all) to see, \nفَاَمَّا مَنْ طَغٰىۙ‏(37)\n\nThen, for such as had transgressed all bounds, \nوَاٰثَرَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ۙ‏(38)\n\nAnd had preferred the life of this world, \nفَاِنَّ الْجَحِيْمَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(39)\n\nThe Abode will be Hell-Fire; \nوَاَمَّا مَنْ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهٖ وَ نَهَى النَّفْسَ عَنِ الْهَوٰىۙ‏(40)\n\nAnd for such as had entertained the fear of standing before their Lord's (tribunal) and had restrained (their) soul from lower desires, \nفَاِنَّ الْجَنَّةَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(41)\n\nTheir abode will be the Garden. \nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ السَّاعَةِ اَيَّانَ مُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ‏(42)\n\nThey ask thee about the Hour, 'When will be its appointed time? \nفِيْمَ اَنْتَ مِنْ ذِكْرٰٮهَاؕ‏(43)\n\nWherein art thou (concerned) with the declaration thereof? \nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ مُنْتَهٰٮهَاؕ‏(44)\n\nWith thy Lord in the Limit fixed therefor. \nاِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُنْذِرُ مَنْ يَّخْشٰٮهَاؕ‏(45)\n\nThou art but a Warner for such as fear it. \nكَاَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْنَهَا لَمْ يَلْبَثُوْۤا اِلَّا عَشِيَّةً اَوْ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(46)\n\nThe Day they see it, (It will be) as if they had tarried but a single evening, or (at most till) the following morn! ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Naazea’at (Those Who Pull Out)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 42 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of entities in the Heavens."
